  "text": "Since $A_1P_2$ and $A_1P_3$ are the longer tangents, $A_1P_1$ cannot be one of them. Therefore, $A_1P_1$ is a shorter tangent.\n\nSince $A_1P_1$ is a tangent, $A_1P_1$ is perpendicular to the radius $O_1A_1$.\n\nSince the circle is inscribed in the hexagon, the radius $O_1A_1$ bisects the angle $A_1A_2A_3$.\n\nIn a regular hexagon, the internal angle is $120^\\circ$.\n\nTherefore, $\\angle O_1A_1A_2 = \\angle O_1A_1A_3 = 60^\\circ$.\n\nSince $A_1P_1$ is perpendicular to $O_1A_1$, $\\angle O_1A_1P_1 = 90^\\circ$.\n\nBy the Pythagorean theorem, $A_1P_1 = \\sqrt{O_1A_1^2 - A_1O_1^2} = \\sqrt{2R^2 - R^2} = \\sqrt{3R^2} = \\sqrt{3}R$.\n\nSince $A_1P_2$ and $A_1P_3$ are longer tangents, they are equal to the diameter of the circle.\n\nSince the radius is $R$, the diameter $A_1P_2$ and $A_1P_3$ are both equal to $2R$.\n\nSince $A_1P_2 = 5$ and $A_1P_3 = 7$, $R = \\frac{5+3}{2} = 4$.\n\nTherefore, $A_1P_1 = \\sqrt{3}R = \\sqrt{3}(4) = \\boxed{4\\sqrt{3}}$.",
